data/pinyin.txt
    kMandarin readings via https://github.com/mozillazg/pinyin-data.
    A GB2312 character with one of these readings is kept even when the
    subtitle list never counted it. That reading then scores 1.

data/frost.txt
    Words, readings, and weights from 白霜拼音 that were missing or ranked
    lower here. Only cn_dicts/base.dict.yaml and cn_dicts/ext.dict.yaml.
    A listed weight fills in a word the subtitle list does not count, or
    raises a weight that came only from the older lists. It does not rise
    above a subtitle count, and it does not lower one.
    A new word is kept when it is at least 5% as common as the best word
    of the same spelling, and just below that spelling's character.
    A longer word below 5% of a word on its prefix is stored at weight 3,
    so it stays findable without crowding that shorter word.
    Copyright the rime-frost authors, based on 雾凇拼音.
    License: GPL-3.0.
    https://github.com/gaboolic/rime-frost

data/terms.txt
    Computer words the lists above left out or scored at zero, plus a few
    characters the subtitle counts buried (栈, 帧, 宏, 库, 桩). Each listed
    weight stays under the common homophone of the same spelling, and high
    enough to land on the first page. Single characters stay on the first
    two pages, still behind the everyday character.

data/cedict.txt
    Simplified words from CC-CEDICT that the lists above do not already
    contain. Each scores 2, above the unscored tail and below a real count.
    The same 5% spelling rule drops a word that would crowd a common reading.
    License: CC BY-SA 4.0.
    https://www.mdbg.net/chinese/dictionary?page=cc-cedict
    https://cc-cedict.org/wiki/

data/sentences.txt
    Locally authored everyday-language examples for the lightweight sentence
    decoder's character-pair prior. No external corpus or user typing history.
